From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:05:39 +0000
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: add Intel MIPS (xRX500/GRX350) platform support

Add arch/mips/intel-mips/, a platform for the Intel (formerly Lantiq)
xRX500 family of interAptiv-based network SoCs - GRX330/GRX350/GRX550 -
as found in DSL gateways such as the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560.

Platform characteristics:

 - MIPS interAptiv (MIPS32 R3.5) dual-core / dual-VPE with CM2.5, GIC
   and CPC.

 - EVA (Enhanced Virtual Addressing) segmentation with a non-zero
   PHYS_OFFSET: DDR starts at physical 0x20000000. kernel-entry-init.h
   programs the segmentation control registers to a 2 GiB EVA layout
   and spaces.h/ioremap.h carry the matching address-space constants.

 - The boot chain hands the boot core over already joined to the
   coherence domain and already running a coherent cache attribute, so
   prom.c preserves that state rather than establishing it: it does not
   force Config.K0, does not write GCR_CL_COHERENCE, and does not probe
   the Cluster Power Controller. Nothing that ships on this hardware
   executes the CPCEN write, and every mainline consumer of the CPC is
   behind mips_cpc_present() and reachable only from CPS smp_ops or a
   power-gated idle state, so leaving mips_cpc_probe() uncalled costs
   this platform nothing. DMA coherency is handled in software
   (DMA_NONCOHERENT + per-device dma-noncoherent).

 - The boot loader hands over no device tree, so
   plat_early_init_devtree() takes the blob get_fdt() finds and panics
   when there is none.

 - irq.c registers the CPU IRQ domain and the MIPS GIC; time.c
   initializes the R4K clock event/source from the CPS-probed
   frequency.

This is a forward-port of the 2018 "MIPS: intel-mips: add initial
support for Intel MIPS SoCs" submission by Songjun Wu
<songjun.wu@linux.intel.com>:

  https://lore.kernel.org/all/20180803030237.3366-1-songjun.wu@linux.intel.com/

updated to the v6.18 APIs (of_fdt, strscpy, smp-ops registration, DMA
coherence API) and with Paul Burton's review feedback on that series
addressed: war.h and the cpu_has_* overrides that match generic
defaults are gone, MIPS32R1 support is dropped (the family is R2+
only), fixup_bigphys_addr and plat_publish_devices are removed, and
the redundant __pa_symbol use is cleaned up.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

